---
import TechList from './TechList.astro';
import { links } from '../data/site';

const built = [
  { name: 'Detection', text: 'YOLOv5 detector for live scallops — small, camouflaged, often half-buried.' },
  { name: 'Habitat segmentation', text: 'U-Net classifying every pixel as eelgrass or sand/silt, giving each image a habitat composition.' },
  { name: 'Representation learning', text: 'GeoCLR — contrastive learning that uses each image’s GPS position to learn habitat structure from mostly unlabeled imagery.' },
  { name: 'Integration', text: 'Detections merged with habitat masks to analyze where scallops occur relative to habitat.' },
];

const decisions = [
  { name: 'Single-class over multi-class', text: 'Live, dead, and face-up shell classes were too sparsely labeled; focusing on live scallops concentrated the model on what matters.' },
  { name: 'Structured augmentation for underwater light', text: 'CLAHE contrast correction, HSV color-space transforms, and rotations to counter strobe hotspots, dark corners, and color loss — applied to training data only.' },
  { name: 'Spatially independent evaluation', text: 'Entire survey lines held out, so results reflect new locations, not memorized ones.' },
  { name: 'Right-sized models', text: 'YOLOv5 generalized better than newer, larger variants on a small, specialized dataset.' },
  { name: 'Bias mitigation', text: 'Identified and corrected systematic eelgrass overestimation from vignetting (15% edge crop) and camera viewing geometry.' },
];
---

<article class="rounded-2xl bg-ocean-900 p-6 text-ocean-50 sm:p-10">
  <p class="text-sm text-ocean-100">
    MSc Oceanography thesis · University of Rhode Island, 2026 · with Rhode Island DEM
  </p>
  <h3 class="mt-3 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-3xl">
    Bay Scallop Monitoring with Computer Vision
  </h3>

  <div class="mt-8 grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ocean-100">The problem</h4>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ocean-50/90">
        Bay scallops in Point Judith Pond, Rhode Island, were once a 100,000+ lb/year fishery; today
        numbers are too low to sustain one, and decades of restoration have had limited success.
        Monitoring relies on scuba surveys and manual image review — slow, small-scale, and hard to
        repeat. And because scallop survival is closely tied to eelgrass, counting scallops without
        measuring habitat tells only half the story.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ocean-100">What it revealed</h4>
      <p class="mt-3 text-ocean-50/90">
        Scallops occurred most often in <strong class="text-white">moderate eelgrass cover (30–60%)</strong>
        — less in sparse or dense beds. That fits a balance between protection from predators
        (lacking in sparse beds) and water exchange and oxygen (reduced in dense ones): habitat
        <em>density</em> matters, not just presence.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4 class="mt-10 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ocean-100">What I built</h4>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-ocean-50/90">
    An end-to-end deep learning pipeline that finds scallops <em>and</em> measures the habitat
    around them, from seafloor imagery collected by an autonomous surface vehicle along RI
    DEM-selected transects.
  </p>
  <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    {
      built.map((b) => (
        <li class="rounded-lg bg-white/5 p-4 ring-1 ring-white/10">
          <p class="font-semibold text-white">{b.name}</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ocean-50/80">{b.text}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <h4 class="mt-10 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-ocean-100">Engineering decisions</h4>
  <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4">
    {
      decisions.map((d) => (
        <div>
          <dt class="font-semibold text-white">{d.name}</dt>
          <dd class="mt-1 text-ocean-50/80">{d.text}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <div class="[&_li]:bg-white/10 [&_li]:text-ocean-50 [&_p]:text-ocean-100">
    <TechList label="Tools" items={['Python', 'OpenCV', 'MATLAB', 'CVAT', 'YOLOv5', 'U-Net', 'GeoCLR']} />
  </div>

  <div class="mt-10 border-t border-white/10 pt-6">
    <p class="text-sm text-ocean-100">
      Data collected with RI DEM; project led by Dr. Chris Roman, URI Graduate School of Oceanography.
    </p>
    <a href={links.thesis} class="mt-3 inline-block font-medium text-white underline decoration-ocean-500 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-white">
      Read the full thesis on DigitalCommons@URI →
    </a>
  </div>
</article>
